rows.41:1194:
So, we're finally down to the last story, huh.
The seventh one still hasn't shown up after all this time...
I wonder if they forgot.{p}

rows.41:349c:
Mr. Kondo wouldn't see her at school, so she looked up his address and lay in wait outside the apartment where he lived alone.
Women in love are scary, huh?
Mr. Kondo was at his wits' end, and in the end he even got down on his hands and knees and begged, apparently.{p}

rows.41:40f0:
Just then, Mr. Kondo felt eyes on his back.
A cold gaze that stabbed right into him.
With a bad feeling, he slowly turned around...{p}

rows.41:4180:
And there was Hirai.
Leaning against the faculty room door, she was glaring coldly at Mr. Kondo from the shadows.
And when their eyes met, she suddenly ran away.{p}

rows.41:44b4:
For whatever reason, Hirai ran into the gym.
Thinking about it later, maybe she was luring Mr. Kondo the whole time.
I mean, as fast as Hirai was, if she'd really wanted to get away, she could have easily.{p}

rows.41:4a28:
With that, Hirai suddenly pulled out a knife.
"...Wh-what are you doing?"
Mr. Kondo was startled.{p}

rows.41:4be0:
With the knife stuck into the base, she twisted it around, digging and gouging.
And with a blank face, as if she felt nothing at all.
The one who was shocked was Mr. Kondo.{p}

rows.41:4f98:
"Ah... AAAAAAAAAGH!"
Mr. Kondo must have been really scared, I think.
He mustered the last of his strength and ran.{p}
